<title>HUNGARY: NABI H1 '97 PRE-TAX PROFIT $2.3MLN.</title>
<headline>NABI H1 '97 PRE-TAX PROFIT $2.3MLN.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of US dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>				Jan-June 1997     Jan-Dec 1996 (*)</p>
<p>    Operating profit	2,228	 vs    3,203</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  2,297	 vs    3,551</p>
<p>    Net sales		49,406	 vs   77,833</p>
<p>    Direct cost of sales 41,875	 vs   67,771</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    7,531	 vs   10,062</p>
<p>    General, admin costs  5,303	 vs    6,859</p>
<p>    Net other income	  391 profit vs     832 profit</p>
<p>    Interest expense	  322	 vs	484</p>
<p>    Taxation		    294	 vs	403</p>
<p>    Earnings per share ($)    0.72    vs	  1.14</p>
<p>NOTE - North American Bus Industries Rt (NABI) assembles buses in Alabama, U.S., from Hungarian-built bodies and chassis mainly for the U.S. market.</p>
<p>(*) Comparative figures for the first half of 1996 were not available. The figures are unaudited, consolidated, and were calculated in accordance with U.S. GAAP rules.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
